WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.020
This March, Netflix is heating up its line-up
with more original movies and TV shows than

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.650
you can shake a Fire Stick at.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:09.090
"Whoa!"

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:13.950
We're staring down the barrel over 50 new
original releases, including new seasons of

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:19.090
Jessica Jones, Santa Clarita Diet, and A Series
of Unfortunate Events — and that's just

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.090
the beginning.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:25.250
Here's everything to look forward to on Netflix
in March 2018, starting with the Netflix originals.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.230
21 Thunder: Season 1

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:32.550
Netflix is kicking off the month with 21 Thunder,
a dramatic sports series that centered on

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.670
a fictional soccer team called the Montreal
Thunder.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.140
From the trailer, it looks like a Friday Night
Lights for the soccer crowd, following the

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.960
players and coaches through the drama of their
personal lives both on and off the field.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.280
Queue up Season 1 on March 1st.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.469
Flint Town

00:00:48.469 --> 00:00:53.800
The town of Flint, Michigan, made headlines
in 2014 when officials discovered that over

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.000
100,000 people had been exposed to contaminated
water.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.140
Now, Netflix is centering a new documentary
series on the controversial burg from a different

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.759
angle — Flint Town follows the town's law
enforcement as they deal with crime, violence,

00:01:05.759 --> 00:01:08.350
and outrage in the wake of the water crisis.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.819
Tune in for every nail-biting moment on March
2nd.

00:01:11.819 --> 00:01:13.850
Girls Incarcerated: Season 1

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:18.490
This new documentary series goes behind bars
in juvenile women's prisons to follow the

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:20.289
day-to-day lives of their young inmates.

00:01:20.289 --> 00:01:23.080
"I've been locked up in and out for like,
four years."

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:23.960
"Six months…"

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:24.960
"For a year and three days."

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:29.740
Season 1 of Girls Incarcerated arrives on
March 2nd, so tune in for all the drama the

00:01:29.749 --> 00:01:32.619
justice system has to offer.

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:33.619
Ravenous

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:39.590
Also known by its original title of Les Affames,
Ravenous is a Canadian drama about a small

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:44.619
group of survivors in rural Quebec struggling
to survive against a zombie hoard.

00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:50.039
Ravenous debuted at the 2017 Toronto International
Film Festival to generous reviews and walked

00:01:50.039 --> 00:01:52.579
away with the award for Best Canadian Film.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:56.079
There's not much more hype we can give it,
so check it out when it hits Netflix on the

00:01:56.079 --> 00:01:57.289
second of the month.

00:01:57.289 --> 00:02:00.249
The World’s Most Extraordinary Homes: Season
1

00:02:00.249 --> 00:02:03.859
Think you've got a crazy home just because
you spent your life savings on lawn flamingos?

00:02:03.859 --> 00:02:06.030
"Well, there's something you don't see every
day."

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:10.229
"I tried to think of the most harmless thing
---- something I loved from my childhood."

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.329
Well, think again.

00:02:11.329 --> 00:02:15.269
This Netflix rebranding of the BBC Two show
takes a stunning look at some of the most

00:02:15.269 --> 00:02:20.290
radical residences on the planet, from architectural
wonders nestled deep in the woods to extravagant

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.540
island retreats.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.079
Check out Season 1 on March 5th.

00:02:24.079 --> 00:02:26.409
Jessica Jones: Season 2

00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:30.450
As one of the original Marvel shows on Netflix,
fans have been waiting for a second season

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:35.459
of Jessica Jones since 2015, only to feel
their souls constrict a little more every

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:36.540
year it didn't happen.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.859
Well, the long, bitter wait is over.

00:02:38.859 --> 00:02:43.469
Tune in for more episodes of everyone's favorite
alcoholic superheroine on March 8.

00:02:43.469 --> 00:02:45.920
"You drinking to remember or forget?"

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.799
"Giving a s--- won't get you a better tip."

00:02:47.799 --> 00:02:51.219
Bad Guys: Vile City: Season 1

00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:56.030
This South Korean crime thriller is a direct
spinoff of the 2014 award-winning series Bad

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:01.060
Guys, which saw three criminals released from
prison to help track down even worse criminals.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:05.700
Bad Guys: Vile City follows the same premise
with a new cast, and looks just as riveting

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.109
as the original series.

00:03:07.109 --> 00:03:09.680
Check it out on March 8th.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:10.879
Ladies First

00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:15.970
If you follow Olympic archery, you'll probably
recognize the name Deepika Kumari, one of

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.390
the top female archers in the world.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:22.969
Ladies First is a new documentary that exposes
Kumari's roots to the streets of India and

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:27.569
traces her hard-fought journey from poverty
to one of the world's most elite athletes.

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:31.829
Tune in for what's bound to be an emotional
journey on March 8th.

00:03:31.829 --> 00:03:33.249
Collateral

00:03:33.249 --> 00:03:38.249
For high-octane murder mystery thrills, look
no further than Collateral, a limited series

00:03:38.249 --> 00:03:42.580
about an assassination on the streets of London
and a police detective who's certain that

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.969
there's more to the story than meets the eye.

00:03:44.969 --> 00:03:48.969
Starring Mudbound's Carey Mulligan, Collateral
looks like a sleek, thrilling mystery that'll

00:03:48.969 --> 00:03:51.190
keep you hooked until the last episode.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:53.650
Find out when it premieres on March 9th.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.730
Love: Season 3

00:03:55.730 --> 00:04:01.340
In this comedy series created by Judd Apatow,
Paul Rust and Gillian Jacobs star as Gus and

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:05.519
Mickey, two twenty-somethings caught up in
a neurotic whirlwind of modern romance.

00:04:05.519 --> 00:04:10.340
You can experience all the ups and downs when
Season 3 of Love drops on March 9th.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.340
A.I.C.O.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.580
Incarnation: Season 1

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:17.930
Netflix is rolling out a good half dozen new
anime series in March, and one of the most

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.829
exciting looks to be A.I.C.O Incarnation.

00:04:20.829 --> 00:04:25.680
This futuristic sci-fi story starts with an
experiment gone wrong that creates an oozing

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.750
AI monstrosity called Matter that's threatening
to destroy the city… and maybe the world.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:35.280
Now, it's up to a bionic 15-year-old girl
named Aico to save everyone.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.930
Strap on your roller skates and mark your
calendar for March 9th.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:43.440
My Next Guest Needs No Introduction With David
Letterman: Malala Yousafzai

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:47.729
In the previous two installments of David
Letterman's well-received hour-long talk show,

00:04:47.729 --> 00:04:51.669
the late-night maven sat down with Barack
Obama and George Clooney.

00:04:51.669 --> 00:04:57.150
This month, Letterman is hosting a one-on-one
with Malala Yousafzai, the youngest person

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.430
to ever be awarded the Nobel Peace Prize.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:03.039
Take a look when the newest episode lands
on March 9th.

00:05:03.039 --> 00:05:05.060
Nailed It: Season 1

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:09.680
Netflix calls this cooking competition show
"part reality contest, part hot mess," which

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.830
doesn't sound like your average cooking show.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:13.060
"Can't forget the vodka."

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:18.270
The show hand picks a group of terrible bakers
and pits them against each other in a culinary

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:21.199
cook-off for a $10,000 grand prize.

00:05:21.199 --> 00:05:24.720
Tune in for all the mayhem on March 9th.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:25.889
The Outsider

00:05:25.889 --> 00:05:31.169
Starring Jared Leto as a soldier forced to
begin working for the yakuza in exchange for

00:05:31.169 --> 00:05:36.210
his freedom, The Outsider definitely looks
like an epic story with some seriously brutal

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.449
action sequences.

00:05:37.449 --> 00:05:39.160
Look for it on March 9th.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:41.780
Terrace House: Opening New Doors: Part 1

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:46.419
The premise of this Japanese language reality
series is instantly familiar — a group of

00:05:46.419 --> 00:05:49.130
young people live in a house filled with cameras.

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:53.520
But rather than the fights and drama of similar
shows like The Real World or Big Brother,

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.050
there isn't a lot that happens in Terrace
House.

00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:58.500
It's just six people being pretty nice to
each other.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:02.800
For 30 minutes at a time, you can watch a
group of people sitting around watching TV,

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.150
eating, and awkwardly making eye contact.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:07.889
Where will Terrace House: Opening New Doors
take us?

00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:12.629
The suspense is gently, apologetically killing
us, but we'll all just have to wait until

00:06:12.629 --> 00:06:14.800
March 13th to find out.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.340
Tabula Rasa: Season 1

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.180
This series centers on a woman with total
amnesia who finds out that she's the prime

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.400
suspect in a murder investigation.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.910
To convince the police that she had nothing
to do with the murder, she has to dig into

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.199
her subconscious to prove that she's innocent.

00:06:29.199 --> 00:06:33.520
It looks like a trippy, psychological ride,
so don't miss it when Season 1 premieres on

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.580
March 15th.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.810
Take Your Pills

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.330
Can one drug define a generation?

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.870
That's the question asked by Take Your Pills.

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:46.479
Directed by Alison Klayman, this documentary
looks at the excessive use of stimulants like

00:06:46.479 --> 00:06:49.310
Ritalin and Adderall in schools and workplaces.

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:51.740
Queue it up on March 16th.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:53.039
Wild Wild Country

00:06:53.039 --> 00:06:59.039
In 1981, an Indian guru began building a city
in Oregon, planning to turn the fringe community

00:06:59.039 --> 00:07:00.710
into a desert utopia.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:04.979
The group was later found to be behind the
largest bioterrorist attack in US history

00:07:04.979 --> 00:07:07.560
and a plot to assassinate a government official.

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:12.009
Wild Wild Country is an unforgettable journey
through the group's formation and their later

00:07:12.009 --> 00:07:13.009
downfall.

00:07:13.009 --> 00:07:15.600
Look for it on Netflix on March 16th.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:17.599
On My Block: Season 1

00:07:17.599 --> 00:07:21.919
In urban L.A., four teenagers struggle to
fit in at their new high school while dealing

00:07:21.919 --> 00:07:23.639
with life in the inner city.

00:07:23.639 --> 00:07:28.190
That's the premise for On My Block, a new
comedy from the creator of MTV's Awkward.

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:31.030
The first season arrives on March 16th.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:32.889
Edha: Season 1

00:07:32.889 --> 00:07:37.629
There's a lot going on in the trailers for
Edha, an Argentinian series focused on the

00:07:37.629 --> 00:07:42.490
dark side of the Buenos Aires fashion industry,
but the main takeaway is that this is shaping

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.670
up to be a gritty, brutal show.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:48.170
In a world of greed and betrayal, who can
you really trust?

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.210
Find out on March 16th.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:52.370
The Legacy of a Whitetail Deer Hunter

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:57.190
Plot details about The Legacy of a Whitetail
Deer Hunter have been few and far between,

00:07:57.190 --> 00:08:01.490
but all we need to know is that it stars Danny
McBride and Josh Brolin, and it was produced

00:08:01.490 --> 00:08:03.370
by the folks behind Eastbound &amp; Down.

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:05.159
Should be an interesting ride.

00:08:05.159 --> 00:08:10.930
The movie is scheduled to premiere at the
2018 SXSW Film Festival before its March 16th

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:13.039
launch on Netflix.

00:08:13.039 --> 00:08:14.379
Layla M.

00:08:14.379 --> 00:08:19.600
Politically charged and culturally relevant,
Layla M. is a story about an 18-year-old Muslim

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:23.030
girl living in Amsterdam who's dealt with
discrimination her whole life.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:27.389
But when she marries a man with ties to a
Middle Eastern Islamic cell, her whole world

00:08:27.389 --> 00:08:28.389
changes.

00:08:28.389 --> 00:08:31.440
Tune in for the riveting journey on March
23rd.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.090
Requiem: Season 1

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:38.890
Originally aired on BBC One, Requiem is a
fantasy thriller about a young woman who heads

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:42.870
out to a small village in the country to find
answers about her past.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:47.380
There, she discovers a supernatural force
that may threaten everything she's ever known.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:51.010
Take a look when Season 1 hits Netflix on
March 23rd.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.770
Roxanne Roxanne

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:57.320
Written and directed by Michael Larnell, this
Netflix original movie tells the true story

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:02.560
of Roxanne Shante, a female rapper who became
a legend of hip hop in the mid '80s.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.090
Roxanne Roxanne follows the teenage MC through
her early years and chronicles her rise to

00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:08.090
fame.

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:10.660
Get with the beat on March 23rd.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:12.380
Game Over, Man!

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:16.820
From the team behind Workaholics comes one
of the most anticipated Netflix films of early

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:22.920
2018 — Game Over, Man!

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:27.590
The Workaholics crew star as three slacker
waiters who have to rise to the challenge

00:09:27.590 --> 00:09:30.720
when the hotel where they work is taken over
by terrorists.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.380
Tune in for the laughs on March 23rd.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.910
Santa Clarita Diet: Season 2

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:40.380
This zombie comedy starring Drew Barrymore
and Timothy Olyphant received rave reviews

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:44.480
over the course of its first season, leaving
fans clamoring for a second almost from the

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:45.480
beginning.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.260
It may have taken a year, but their wishes
have finally been answered.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:50.470
Look for it on March 23rd.

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:52.280
The Mechanism: Season 1

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:57.630
Loosely based on a real-life corporate scandal,
The Mechanism is a scripted drama series that

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.440
looks into corruption and greed.

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:03.940
With Narcos executive producer Jose Padilha
as showrunner, you know it's going to be a

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:04.940
crazy ride.

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:07.080
Take a look on March 23rd.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:10.750
Lemony Snicket's A Series of Unfortunate Events:
Season 2

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:15.130
Winding down the month, Netflix is rolling
out the second season of A Series of Unfortunate

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:20.230
Events, with the events of books five through
nine as the main focus of the upcoming season.

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:24.650
If you can't get enough of Count Olaf and
the Baudelaire orphans, mark your calendar.

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:27.200
"Premiering March 30th.

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:28.120
Cheers!"

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:30.880
Rapture

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:35.380
Netflix is doubling down on their hip hop
history with Rapture, an eight-part documentary

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:39.320
series that takes a magnifying glass to the
biggest rap stars on the planet.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:44.380
If you've ever wondered what goes on in the
personal lives of celebs like 2 Chainz, G-Eazy,

00:10:44.380 --> 00:10:49.770
and A Boogie wit da Hoodie, you'll finally
get your chance to find out on March 30th.

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:51.060
First Match

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:55.760
Continuing their theme of female empowerment
in honor of International Women's Day, Netflix

00:10:55.760 --> 00:11:00.010
is releasing this hard-hitting drama about
a teenage girl who joins an all-boys wrestling

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.010
team.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:05.010
The movie is based on a short film of the
same name that won some awards in 2000.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.110
Look for it on March 30th.

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:08.660
Happy Anniversary

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:12.940
In this indie comedy, a young couple take
a hard look at their marriage and try to decide

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:16.080
whether they want to get a divorce on their
three year anniversary.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:18.680
"Happy anniversary."

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:20.820
"Yeah!"

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:26.700
Happy Anniversary stars Ben Schwartz and Noel
Wells, and premieres on March 30.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.630
The Titan

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:32.920
Netflix hasn't promoted this upcoming sci-fi
thriller, but one of the film's writers confirmed

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:36.890
on Twitter that The Titan will indeed be released
as a Netflix original.

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:41.360
Sam Worthington stars as a soldier who gets
genetically altered to survive on Saturn's

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:42.820
moon Titan.

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:46.230
Mark your calendar - The Titan shows up on
March 30th.

00:11:46.230 --> 00:11:48.320
Trailer Park Boys: Season 12

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:52.360
Canada's trailer park heroes are back for
yet another season of their award-winning

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:53.360
comedy series.

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:57.490
Season 12 will see Julian, Ricky, and Bubbles
doing more things than ever.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:12:01.700
"There's two things that dogs don't mix with:
kitties and Bubbles."

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.310
Check it out on March 30th.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:06.560
Trump: An American Dream: Season 1

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:11.151
This month, Netflix is pointing their political
spotlight on the White House with Trump: An

00:12:11.151 --> 00:12:16.300
American Dream, a Netflix rebranding of the
UK-produced documentary about Donald Trump.

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:21.010
The series will dig through over five decades
of the current POTUS' past.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:24.110
Season 1 drops on March 30th.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:25.490
Original stand-up comedy

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:29.791
Keep your eyes peeled for a host of brand
new stand-up comedy specials this March, with

00:12:29.791 --> 00:12:32.160
a heavy focus on international acts.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:37.770
Look for a new special by Adel Karam on March
1st, followed by Malena Pichot and Natalia

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.710
Valdebenito on the 2nd.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:44.860
As the month rolls on, Netflix will drop Gad
Elmaleh: American Dream on the 6th, Ricky

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:50.120
Gervais: Humanity on the 13th, and Season
2 of The Standups on March 20th.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:53.120
If you're looking for laughs, you're definitely
in the right place.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.990
That covers all the Netflix originals.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:13:00.670
Now, let's look at all the other movies and
TV shows coming to Netflix in March 2018.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.580
New movies

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:05.940
Netflix is only bringing in a handful of new
action movies this month.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:12.080
For sword-and-sandals epics, we've got 300
arriving on the 1st and 2017's Troy: The Odyssey

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:13.320
coming on the 12th.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:19.000
On the sci-fi spectrum, look for 2307: Winter's
Dream on the 1st, along with Battle Drone

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.130
and I Am Number Four.

00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:22.740
In the mood for lighter fare?

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:25.300
Netflix is adding a great selection of comedies
in March.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:30.130
The first of the month will see Ghostbusters
1 and 2, Beerfest, and The Bucket List hitting

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:31.420
the streaming service.

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:38.000
Also keep an eye out for Jackass: Number Two
and Jackass 3.5 on the 1st and 15th respectively.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:41.300
There won't be a whole lot of change on the
documentary front this month, but the few

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:44.300
films that are arriving will definitely be
worth watching.

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:50.140
Look for Expedition China on the 4th, Conor
McGregor: Notorious on the 21st, and Red Trees

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:51.510
on the 24th.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:55.970
And if that's not enough drama, Martin Scorsese's
Casino is joining the Netflix ranks on the

00:13:55.970 --> 00:14:01.040
first, along with Gridiron Gang, Moon, Revolutionary
Road, and Up in the Air.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:03.050
Go ahead and take our money now.

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:04.740
"Here, take mine too."

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:09.070
New family arrivals on the first of the month
include the animated adventure comedy Alpha

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:12.320
and Omega and Stuart Little 3: Call of the
Wild.

00:14:12.320 --> 00:14:19.330
On the 6th, relive the classics with 1974's
Benji and the 1977 sequel, For the Love of

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:23.880
Benji — just in time for Netflix's original
Benji reboot on March 16th.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:28.120
Finally, Netflix's new thriller lineup is
heating up along with the weather.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:32.770
All three Cruel Intentions films arrive on
the first, side-by-side with Hostage, The

00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.510
Descent, and The Gift.

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:38.810
Finally, Let Me In is showing up to creep
out audiences at the end of the month.

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:41.660
Look for that on the 31st.

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:43.170
New television

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:47.730
March won't herald the arrival of much new
television, with only five non-Netflix shows

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:49.230
landing throughout the month.

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:54.630
On March 1st, look for the 18th season of
Law &amp; Order: SVU, followed by the second season

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:56.880
of The Hollywood Masters on March 15th.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:01.991
Finally, the month ends with the 2018 season
of Men on a Mission on March 27th and the

00:15:01.991 --> 00:15:06.660
kids' series Miraculous: Tales of Ladybug
&amp; Cat Noir on the 30th.

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:08.110
Thanks for watching!

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:10.910
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:13.020
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

